---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Express Entry Canada Guide for Africans | AfriMigrate"
  description="A plain-language guide to Canada's Express Entry system: the three programs, how draws work, and how African applicants can qualify — 100% free."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/canada">Canada</a> / Express Entry</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Canada · Express Entry</div>
  <h1>Express Entry Guide</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Express Entry is the system Canada uses to manage applications for its three main economic immigration programs. It's the fastest route to permanent residence for most African applicants with a degree, decent English or French, and a few years of skilled work experience.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">The Three Programs</div>
    <h2>Which program fits you?</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Program</th><th>Best for</th><th>Key requirement</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Federal Skilled Worker (FSW)</td><td>Applicants outside Canada with no local work experience</td><td>At least 1 year of skilled work experience, language test, education assessment</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Canadian Experience Class (CEC)</td><td>Applicants who have worked in Canada on a work permit</td><td>At least 1 year of skilled Canadian work experience in the last 3 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Federal Skilled Trades (FST)</td><td>Qualified tradespeople</td><td>2 years of skilled trade experience and a valid job offer or certificate of qualification</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Step by Step</div>
    <h2>How the process works</h2>
    <div class="steps" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">1</div><h3>Check eligibility</h3><p>Confirm you meet the minimum requirements for at least one of the three programs.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">2</div><h3>Get your score</h3><p>Take a language test and get your credentials assessed, then calculate your CRS score.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">3</div><h3>Submit your profile</h3><p>Enter the Express Entry pool. Canada runs draws roughly every two weeks.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-icon">4</div><h3>Apply for PR</h3><p>If invited, you have 60 days to submit a complete application with supporting documents.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Boost Your Chances</div>
    <h2>The fastest way in: provincial nomination</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      General Express Entry draws can require CRS scores above 500 in a competitive year. A provincial nomination adds 600 points, which all but guarantees an invitation at the next draw. Most African applicants who don't score highly enough for general draws get in this way.
    </p>
    <a href="/canada/pnp" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Check Provincial Nominee Programs →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Next Step</div>
    <h2>Know your number</h2>
    <p class="lead">Before anything else, calculate your CRS score so you know exactly where you stand.</p>
    <a href="/canada/crs-calculator" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Calculate my CRS score →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
